WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.900
A Notice from the Yamayuri Council
When watching
"Maria Watches Over Us ~Printemps~,"
please have the room brightly lit and
sit well away from the television set.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:10.400
I am sorry.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.370
The day we said we would go
to the amusement park...

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.300
I believe it was next Sunday, right?

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:18.640
Yes...

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.740
Could it be that it does not
work for you anymore?

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.220
Amusement Park Date

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.590
Amusement Park Date
Yes, well...

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:26.140
Amusement Park Date

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.120
If it's about me, please do not worry.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:31.420
Really?

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.590
It's such a help that you're
an understanding little sister.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.830
Do you have some business to attend to?

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.400
Perhaps something to do
with your father's work?

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:41.600
No...

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.200
Then, is it family related?

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.910
Well, if anything, I suppose
that would be the way to put it.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:53.350
Speaking of your family, is Sayako Oba-san well?

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:54.610
Yes.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.010
And your father?

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.840
Both my father and grandfather are well.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.080
But, what of it?

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.220
No, I just thought I would ask.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:06.460
I see.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.720
See you then.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:14.330
Sachiko Onee-sama.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.670
Oh, Yumi-sama, good day.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:21.610
G-Good day, Toko-chan.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:50.640
The maidens, who flock to
Maria-sama's garden,

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.410
pass through the tall gates today yet
again with innocent, angelic smiles.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:02:00.210
Their pure hearts and bodies are
clad in deep-colored uniforms.

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:03.080
So that the pleats of their
skirts are not disturbed...

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.510
...and so that their white sailor
collars are not set aflutter,

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.890
it is customary here to walk
slowly and with decorum.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.390
The Private Lillian Girls' Academy,
a garden of maidens.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.410
Maria Watches Over Us
Printemps

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:37.520
In the morning mist,
Asamoya no naka

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:44.460
the white path goes on.
tsuzuku shiroi michi

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:51.960
The birds sing.
Tori no saezuri

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:59.630
We exchange greetings.
Aisatsu kawashinagara

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:07.080
At times, the clouds hang low,
Toki ni kumo ga tarekomete

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:14.560
and the sun may grow dim.
hizashi kagerou tomo

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:22.660
But I will walk with my chin up,
Sesuji nobashite aruku

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:30.210
for I know,
watashi wa shitteru kara

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:37.180
that above those heavy clouds...
omoi kumo no ue wa

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:45.110
...is the blue sky.
aoi sora

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:51.920
Rainy Blue

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.270
Even on days when it rains,

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:08.680
when I think of how I'll get to
use my favorite umbrella,

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.900
I don't find it unpleasant.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:15.940
Fukuzawa

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:17.340
Yumi-san. Yumi-san.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.580
Minako-sama...

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:28.290
Over there.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.200
That girl.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.490
She's the one from the Maria Festival, right?

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.000
Matsudaira Toko-san.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:40.910
What's going on here?

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.240
"What's going on?"

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.480
In truth, I'd almost like to ask that myself.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.350
They are apparently related.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.030
Related? Don't you think they're
overly familiar with each other?

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.360
She comes by every day, chatting away.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:00.790
E-Every day?

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.090
So, just as I suspected, you didn't know.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.120
So, would it be all right?

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:08.070
I swear, I will not get in your way,
Sachiko Onee-sama.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.700
No, this is not for fun.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:14.830
Toko would be happy, just to be
able to go on a drive together.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.670
A drive? What could it be about?

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.010
This will not work, Minako-sama.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:23.080
Provoking me will not result
in some kind of incident.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.050
Though, if I were to get jealous...

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.560
...and make a grab for Toko-chan
with tears in my eyes,

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.590
you might be able to slap on a
title like "Red Rose Revolution,"

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.460
and you would have your story...

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:34.530
I wasn't anticipating anything of the sort.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:35.320
What?

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:40.870
I don't want your relationship
with Sachiko-san to fall apart.

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:45.370
So I thought I would take action early
and that was why I brought you here.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:46.840
Take action?

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.670
Watching you reminds me...

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.110
Of what?

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:55.780
My friend.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:57.780
Your friend?

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:03.110
Yes, a classmate of mine whose
big sister was two-timing her.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.150
Two-timing?!

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.260
She knew about it,
but she pretended not to notice.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.660
She was probably too proud.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.760
What happened to her?

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.030
Nothing. She just let it lie.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:19.670
But she spent her three years in
high school with negative emotions...

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.940
...and in the end, her anger exploded,

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.400
and when her big sister was graduating,

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:27.410
she threw the rosary at her...
and that was the end.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.380
The end...

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.550
I'm not saying that Sachiko-san
is being unfaithful to you.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:37.150
Nor am I advocating that
you throw the rosary at her.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.750
But I don't think putting up
with it is your only option.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.300
She should have pressed her for answers,
instead of just waiting.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.300
This is me being a busybody.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:51.770
I just don't want you to have
to put on a fake smile.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.040
Fake...

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:02.040
Certainly, what Minako-sama said might be right...

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:06.640
After being told that I was an
understanding little sister,

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:09.950
I just can't bring myself to be demanding,
so I've been restraining myself...

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.760
But that will all be over tomorrow.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:20.260
Because tomorrow is the day of the
long-awaited amusement park date!

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:24.260
Because that day is finally going to come!

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:28.700
Amusement Park Date
Amusement Park Date

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.580
What are you twirling for?

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:47.830
You're that happy about
going on a date with Sachiko-san?

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.450
I am happy.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.020
I'm relieved.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.330
About what?

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:56.160
Because you know, you'd been downcast lately.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.100
Really?

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.310
Thank you for worrying about me.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.510
But I'm all better now.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:06.850
W-What?

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:12.320
I guess your life at school
revolves around Sachiko-san, huh?

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:13.710
Yes, it does.

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:15.450
We're soeurs, after all.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:17.290
Why?

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.650
I don't know how to put it... It's like...

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:22.420
You're dependent on her or something...

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:24.890
It's just got me a little worried.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.130
Worried?

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.930
Nah, I'm probably worried for nothing.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:30.200
Don't let it bug you too much.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.880
Yumi-chan, it's from Ogasawara-san!

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:44.280
Here.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:45.770
Right...

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.180
This is Yumi speaking.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:50.590
This is Sachiko.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:54.030
I am sorry, Yumi. About today...

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.060
Are you unable to go?

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:00.540
Yes, something suddenly came up.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.870
With the way this date had
been postponed already,

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.840
I had made sure to keep
today free far in advance, but...

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.570
I was looking forward to this too, you know.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:10.900
You're awful, Onee-sama!

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:13.340
How many times do you think this makes?!

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.350
Now that you have canceled our date,

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:17.780
where do you plan to go and to do what?!

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.110
Are you meeting with someone?

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:22.710
Is that person someone you
must prioritize before me?!

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.720
I understand.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.420
I am so sorry. Bye.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.070
Yumi...

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:41.670
I won't be going out today.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.350
Amusement Park Date
Amusement Park Date

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.950
Amusement Park Date
Amusement Park Date

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.500
Good day, Yumi-sama.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:17.300
Good day.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:24.520
If you are here to visit the Rose
Mansion, why don't you come in?

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:25.920
It's all right.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.380
I only dropped by in the hopes
of seeing her for a moment.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.350
Oh, Toko-chan.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.860
Rosa Chinensis. Here.

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:41.530
Oh, you went to the trouble of
bringing it for me? Thank you.

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:46.910
I dropped by your class during break,
but you weren't there, so...

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:49.000
It was an optional class.

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:52.840
Why does Toko-chan have
my Onee-sama's watch?

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:54.200
Something she forgot?

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:58.120
But when and where did
my Onee-sama forget it?

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:05.020
Well then, good day, Rosa Chinensis.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:06.380
Good day.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:14.800
Yumi, I am so sorry about yesterday.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.140
Not at all...

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:27.820
"Just as hydrangeas flower in
endless layers, may you live as long."

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:30.980
"Each time I look upon them,
I shall think of you, my love."

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:34.720
To think she broke her
promise with me yesterday...

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:36.490
...to meet with Toko-chan.

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:39.920
Do you know how else
hydrangeas are referred to?

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:43.960
You all know how hydrangeas
change in color, right?

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:46.670
Perhaps because of that,
in the language of flowers,

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:49.970
it seems they are called
"change of heart" or " fickleness."

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:51.800
"Fickleness"...

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.210
Just as the color of the
hydrangea blossoms change,

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:03.140
can people's hearts change color as well?

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:35.750
Are you going home?

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:37.350
Yes.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:39.950
Since I have reached a good stopping point.

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:42.750
The next...

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:46.260
Please set the next date.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:48.460
The next?

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:49.730
Together...

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:54.630
You said that we'd go to
the amusement park together.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:57.800
I cannot set any dates,

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:01.100
because I may end up having to cancel again.

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:03.330
Even so, please set the next date!

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:08.670
Because if you set the next date,
I can feel at ease until that day.

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:11.550
I do not care if you end up having to cancel.

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:14.450
If you set a date, until that day, I can...

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.300
Sachiko Onee-sama.

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:34.470
All right.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:41.880
Onee-sama, we are still in the
middle of our conversation.

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:46.650
Toko-chan, go on downstairs and wait for me.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:47.410
Certainly.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:57.530
Yumi, I cannot make any plans right now,
so I cannot set a date with you.

00:13:58.030 --> 00:13:59.660
Then, when will you be able to?

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.800
I don't know.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:03.130
Onee-sama...

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:04.830
Please be reasonable.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.030
Please don't go.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:14.540
Please don't go, Onee-sama!

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:16.720
Rosa Chinensis!

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:21.250
So you would choose Toko-chan over me?!

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:24.080
That's crossing the line!

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:42.570
What a twisted-up person I am...

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.910
Begging her unreasonably to make a promise,

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:47.470
and purposefully saying
things that will anger her...

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:11.030
Yumi...

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:13.400
Where's your umbrella?
What happened to your umbrella?

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:15.270
Did you lose it?

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:18.400
Don't just...

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.840
...take things that belong to other people...

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:23.810
Yumi...

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:27.150
Don't rob me of the things...

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.210
...that are precious to me!

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.860
Sunday has come again.

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:42.860
A Sunday without an engagement
with my Onee-sama...

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.370
I have to apologize about the other day.

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:51.180
This is the Ogasawara residence.

00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:53.410
My name is Fukuzawa.

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:56.210
Is Sachiko-sama there?

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:58.040
One moment, please.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.720
So, she's there...

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:05.050
Hello? Yumi-chan?

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:06.450
Um...

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.600
This is Kashiwagi. It's been a long time.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:12.020
Oh yes, it has been a long time.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:16.660
Sacchan is home, but she
can't come to the phone.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.160
She got a bit car sick, so she's resting.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:21.140
Car?

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:24.680
I'll say this, so you don't get the wrong idea,

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:28.420
but it's not as if she and
I went out for a drive alone.

00:16:28.950 --> 00:16:31.280
Toko was with us too, so don't worry.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:32.540
Toko-chan was?

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:36.250
Yes. Even now, Toko is looking after Sacchan,

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:37.790
so you can rest easy and leave things to her.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.950
Like me? She won't even let me in the room.

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:42.820
I see...

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.390
Did you need something?

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:48.940
If you have a message, I'll make sure she gets it.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:51.200
Oh, would you rather I let
you talk to Toko instead?

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.740
No, it's nothing urgent,

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:55.440
so I will talk to her when I see her at school.

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:57.500
Really? Then, bye.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:11.150
This is... the answer...

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:29.970
What in the world happened?!

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:31.910
Why have you stopped coming
to the Rose Mansion?!

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:36.380
Sachiko-sama is worried, too!

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:37.280
Surely not.

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:40.180
It's true.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:43.120
Anyway, let's go to the Rose Mansion now.

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:45.580
I'm not going.

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:50.490
I don't know what happened,
but I'm sure it was Sachiko-sama's fault.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.090
So I'll stand with you in protest.

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:55.570
If you stay angry without saying anything,

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:57.590
you'll never reach reconciliation.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:00.900
We're already beyond that now!

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.570
Thank you for worrying about me.

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:05.940
I'm sorry!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.070
Yumi-san...

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:14.890
Fukuzawa

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:21.320
Yumi.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.550
Onee-sama...

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:33.100
I had a feeling that I would get to see you.

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:40.310
I owe you a proper explanation, don't I?

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:50.950
Yumi.

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:53.590
Onee-sama...

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:58.830
Matsudaira

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:02.300
Sachiko Onee-sama.

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:05.530
Pardon me for making you wait.

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:13.370
So that is it.

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:18.680
Wait, Yumi-sama.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.350
You were still not done talking, right?

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:25.380
We are in a bit of a hurry,
so we can't stand around talking,

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:28.600
but if you wouldn't mind walking with us,

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:30.760
why not continue with your conversation?

00:19:32.470 --> 00:19:35.490
Right, Rosa Chinensis? Let us do that.

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:37.070
Yes.

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:40.400
Yumi, let's walk home together for a ways.

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:42.740
No...

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:44.900
It no longer matters.

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:47.110
Yumi-sama?!

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:18.500
Sei-sama!

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:26.680
Yumi-chan...

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:33.750
What's wrong?

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:35.450
There, there.

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:40.830
Sachiko...

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:51.510
Yumi.

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:03.580
I'm sorry to trouble you.

00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:11.520
Yumi-chan, are you okay with this?

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:14.000
Sachiko's leaving.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:15.570
It's fine.

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:18.670
These...

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:21.060
Sachiko picked them up and handed them to me.

00:21:22.240 --> 00:21:23.710
Sachiko-sama did?

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:26.510
This is what I am...

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:30.270
A miserable umbrella, dropped to the
ground and soiled in muddy water.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:34.080
Sachiko-sama picked it up
and entrusted it to Sei-sama.

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:37.050
She doesn't need it anymore...

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:44.860
Onee-sama!

00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:54.440
Onee-sama!

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:29.170
My relationship with my Onee-sama
is a candle flickering in the wind.

00:23:29.170 --> 00:23:30.100
"A candle flickering in the wind."

00:23:30.100 --> 00:23:31.810
To be in a precarious and short-lived situation,

00:23:31.810 --> 00:23:32.940
the way a wind-blown flame can be extinguished.

00:23:32.940 --> 00:23:34.610
I know they say spilled water
cannot be returned to the platter...

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:35.680
A saying that came from how...

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:37.240
...water spilled from a platter cannot be restored.

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:39.580
But they also say even a dog will
not interfere in a marital spat...

00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:42.020
Marital spats often begin over trivial matters...

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.520
...and if an outsider unwisely tries to mediate,

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:44.450
he will only end up looking like a fool.

00:23:44.450 --> 00:23:46.190
So it means, "Keep at it for all we care!"

00:23:46.190 --> 00:23:48.180
Is that the kind of thing this episode is about?

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:48.990
Next time on "Maria Watches Over Us,"

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:49.990
Next time on "Maria Watches Over Us,"
Next Time "The Blue Umbrella"

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:50.760
"The Blue Umbrella".
Next Time "The Blue Umbrella"

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:52.130
A picture is worth a thousand words.
Next Time "The Blue Umbrella"

00:23:52.130 --> 00:23:53.290
It is apparently better to see it for yourself,
Next Time "The Blue Umbrella"

00:23:53.290 --> 00:23:55.260
than to hear about it
a thousand times from others.
Next Time "The Blue Umbrella"

00:23:55.260 --> 00:23:55.990
Next Time "The Blue Umbrella"
